LeadtrackerDealEvents = Show events in the deal map by default
LeadtrackerDealEventsHelp = Sets the starting position of the "Events" switch on the deal map. When on, calls, emails and meetings (hung off the document they relate to, or the lead) show by default; when off they are hidden until the viewer flips the switch. The switch is always available either way.
LeadtrackerDealEventsToggle = Events
LeadtrackerDealEventsToggleHelp = Show or hide agenda events (calls, emails, meetings) in this deal map.

# Deal map — warranty & calls
LeadtrackerNodeWarranty = Warranty
LeadtrackerNodeRequest = Service request
LeadtrackerNodeCall = Call
LeadtrackerEdgeAux = related
LeadtrackerEdgeCall = call
LeadtrackerDealWarranty = Show warranty records
LeadtrackerDealWarrantyHelp = Add warranty claims and service requests to the deal map as small cards, hung off the order they relate to. Requires the Warranty Service module.
LeadtrackerDealCalls = Show phone calls
LeadtrackerDealCallsHelp = Add phone-call records tied to this project as small cards under the lead. Requires the PBX Calls module.
LeadtrackerDealCallsBroad = Include customer-level calls
LeadtrackerDealCallsBroadHelp = Also show calls matched to this deal's customer (not just calls tagged to this project). Customer-level calls are marked and dimmed. Off = only calls tied to this project.
LeadtrackerCallBroadTag = customer
LeadtrackerCallBroadHelp = Matched to the deal's customer, not tagged to this specific project.
LeadtrackerEventSms = SMS
LeadtrackerDealBroad = Include customer-level correspondence
LeadtrackerDealBroadHelp = Also show calls, emails, SMS and meetings matched to this deal's customer (not just items tagged to this project). Customer-level items are marked and dimmed. Off = only correspondence tied to this project or its documents.
LeadtrackerAttribution = Attribution token
LeadtrackerAttributionHelp = Opaque attribution token recorded when the lead was captured. Written by lead intake; do not edit by hand.
LeadtrackerAttributionCreateFailed = Lead Tracker could not create the attribution field on projects: %s
LeadtrackerWebhookTitle = Outbound stage events
LeadtrackerWebhookHelp = Each time a tracked lead reaches a new pipeline stage, a JSON event (stage, date, lead amount, probability, weighted value, hashed contact and attribution data) is queued and posted to the URL below by a scheduled job. Use it to report lead outcomes to a tag server, an automation tool or an advertising platform. Requires the Scheduled jobs module.
LeadtrackerWebhookEnabled = Send stage events
LeadtrackerWebhookUrl = Destination URL
LeadtrackerWebhookUrlInvalid = The destination URL must be a valid https:// address.
LeadtrackerWebhookSecret = Signing secret
LeadtrackerWebhookSecretHelp = Every request carries an X-Leadtracker-Signature header: the HMAC-SHA256 of the request body computed with this secret. Check it on the receiving end to be sure a call comes from this installation.
LeadtrackerWebhookSecretPending = Generated when the settings are first saved.
LeadtrackerWebhookRegen = Generate a new secret on save (the receiver must be updated)
LeadtrackerWebhookContact = Include contact details in clear
LeadtrackerWebhookContactHelp = By default only SHA-256 hashes of the third party's email and phone are sent. Tick to also send the name, email and phone unhashed.
LeadtrackerWebhookRecent = Recent stage events
LeadtrackerWebhookColStage = Stage
LeadtrackerWebhookNoEvents = No stage event recorded yet.
LeadtrackerWebhookStatusPending = Pending
LeadtrackerWebhookStatusSent = Sent
LeadtrackerWebhookStatusFailed = Failed
LeadtrackerWebhookStatusSkipped = Not sent
LeadtrackerWebhookTest = Send a test event
LeadtrackerWebhookDeliverNow = Deliver pending now
LeadtrackerWebhookRequeue = Retry failed events
LeadtrackerWebhookTestOk = Test event accepted (HTTP %s).
LeadtrackerWebhookTestKo = Test event not accepted: %s
LeadtrackerWebhookDelivered = Delivery run: %s
LeadtrackerWebhookRequeued = %s event(s) put back in the queue.
LeadtrackerCronDeliver = Lead Tracker: deliver stage events
LeadtrackerReportAs = Report as
LeadtrackerReportAsHelp = Report as: what reaching this stage means in outbound stage events. Receiving systems match on this category, so they do not need to know your stage names. "Do not send" keeps the stage in the lead's history without announcing it.
LeadtrackerCategoryNone = Do not send
LeadtrackerCategoryLead = Lead
LeadtrackerCategoryQualified = Qualified lead
LeadtrackerCategoryProgress = Other progress
LeadtrackerCategorySale = Sale
LeadtrackerCategoryLost = Lost
LeadtrackerGoogleTitle = Google Ads conversion file
LeadtrackerGoogleHelp = Publishes a conversions file that Google Ads imports on a schedule, so Google learns which ad clicks became leads and which became sales. In Google Ads, add a scheduled import with an HTTPS source and give it the address, user name and password below. A stage event is included when its "Report as" category has a conversion name below and the lead carries a Google click identifier. Each lead is reported once per conversion.
LeadtrackerGoogleEnabled = Publish the conversion file
LeadtrackerGoogleUrl = File address
LeadtrackerGoogleUser = User name
LeadtrackerGooglePassword = Password
LeadtrackerGoogleRegen = Generate a new password on save (the import in Google Ads must be updated)
LeadtrackerGoogleConvName = Conversion name for "%s"
LeadtrackerGoogleConvNameHelp = Must match the name of a conversion action in Google Ads exactly. Leave empty to leave that category out of the file. A sale is reported at the lead amount; earlier stages at the amount multiplied by the probability.
LeadtrackerGoogleHashed = Add hashed email and phone
LeadtrackerGoogleHashedHelp = Adds SHA-256 hashes of the third party's email and phone as extra columns, for enhanced conversions for leads. Leave off for a click-identifier-only import, which rejects extra columns.
LeadtrackerGoogleConsent = Consent stated in the file
LeadtrackerGoogleConsentHelp = Adds the "Ad User Data" and "Ad Personalization" columns with the same value on every row. Only state what your own consent collection supports.
LeadtrackerGoogleConsentUnset = Not stated
LeadtrackerGoogleConsentGranted = Granted
LeadtrackerGoogleConsentDenied = Denied
LeadtrackerGoogleStats = In the file now (last %s days)
LeadtrackerGoogleStatsDetail = %s conversion(s). Left out: %s without a Google click identifier, %s with no conversion name for their category, %s repeat(s).
LeadtrackerGoogleApiTitle = Google Ads through the Data Manager API
LeadtrackerGoogleApiHelp = Sends the same conversions directly to Google Ads within minutes, instead of waiting for Google to fetch the file. This route also reports clicks that only carry an iOS click identifier, and, when hashed email and phone are enabled above, leads with no click identifier at all. It needs a Google Cloud service account with the Data Manager API enabled, added as a user of the Google Ads account. A conversion sent by both routes is counted once.
LeadtrackerGoogleApiEnabled = Send conversions through the API
LeadtrackerGoogleCustomerId = Google Ads customer ID
LeadtrackerGoogleLoginCustomerId = Manager account ID
LeadtrackerGoogleLoginCustomerIdHelp = Only when the service account was added to a manager account rather than to the account above.
LeadtrackerGoogleActionId = Conversion action ID for "%s"
LeadtrackerGoogleActionIdHelp = The numeric ID of an "import from clicks" conversion action. Leave empty to leave that category out.
LeadtrackerGoogleKey = Service account key
LeadtrackerGoogleKeyHelp = Paste the content of the JSON key file downloaded from Google Cloud. It is stored encrypted and never shown again.
LeadtrackerGoogleKeyStored = Key stored for %s.
LeadtrackerGoogleKeyRemove = Remove it
LeadtrackerGoogleKeyPaste = Paste the JSON key here
LeadtrackerGoogleKeyReplace = Paste a new JSON key here to replace the stored one
LeadtrackerGoogleKeyInvalid = This is not a usable service account key. Paste the whole JSON key file.
LeadtrackerGoogleApiStatus = Conversions sent through the API
LeadtrackerGoogleApiStatusDetail = %s sent, %s waiting for a retry, %s given up.
LeadtrackerGoogleApiTest = Test Google Ads connection
LeadtrackerGoogleApiTestOk = Google accepted the test request: the key, the account access and the conversion action are valid. Nothing was recorded.
LeadtrackerGoogleApiTestKo = Google refused the test request: %s
